# Line endings, decided here instead of by whatever core.autocrlf each clone
# happens to have.
#
# This file exists because `Test windows-latest` was red for a golden test.
# actions/checkout on Windows runs Git for Windows, which defaults to
# core.autocrlf=true and therefore writes testdata/*.golden with CRLF — while
# the renderer under test emits "\n". The comparison is byte for byte, so it
# failed on Windows and nowhere else, and the diff was invisible in a CI log
# (the bytes differ, the rendered text does not).

# Golden files are compared byte for byte. Never translate them.
*.golden -text

# Source and fixtures the toolchain reads: LF everywhere, including Windows
# checkouts. Go itself tolerates CRLF, but gofmt diffs and any test that
# compares file bytes do not.
*.go text eol=lf
*.json text eol=lf
*.toml text eol=lf
*.yml text eol=lf
*.yaml text eol=lf
*.sh text eol=lf

# PowerShell in the Windows harness wants CRLF (see test/windows/README.md's
# gotchas — a BOM-less, LF-only .ps1 is read through the ANSI code page and one
# stray byte becomes a parse error).
*.ps1 text eol=crlf

# Binaries and archives: hands off.
*.png binary
*.ico binary
*.zip binary
*.gz binary
*.exe binary
